# =================================================================
# 📋 MIGRATION GUIDE FROM YOUR CURRENT SETUP:
# =================================================================
# 
# STEP 1: Update your GitHub Actions setup
# - Change DOCKER_REGISTRY to your GitHub username
# - Set up GitHub secrets (see DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md)
# 
# STEP 2: Copy this file to your Hetzner server
# - scp env.hetzner-github-actions.template your-server:/path/to/pessoa/.env
# 
# STEP 3: Replace your current docker-compose file
# - Copy docker-compose.hetzner-github-actions.yml to your server
# - Use this instead of your current docker-compose-hetzner working copy.md
# 
# STEP 4: First deployment
# - Push your code to trigger GitHub Actions
# - GitHub Actions will build and push images
# - SSH to your server and run:
#   docker-compose -f docker-compose.hetzner-github-actions.yml pull
#   docker-compose -f docker-compose.hetzner-github-actions.yml up -d
# 
# BENEFITS:
# ✅ No more building on your Hetzner server (saves time/resources)
# ✅ Automatic deployments when you push code
# ✅ Consistent images across environments
# ✅ Keeps your working mylayer.org:8443 configuration
# ✅ Easy rollbacks with image tags
# ================================================================= 